    // params: whether this test contract should be an admin and a description string
    function run(bool makeAdmin, string calldata description) public payable {
        // set up admin mapping: only external callers can set isAdmin via C's public mapping, but mapping is public and writable only by C itself.
        // The test harness deploys C fresh; we can only interact through c. C exposes 'isAdmin' mapping getter and onlyAdmin modifier protects newEmergencyOracle.
        // We simulate being an admin by directly setting c.isAdmin(address(this)) is not possible. However the contract C has a public mapping isAdmin that is mutable only by C; thus the only way to make this contract an admin is if the freshly deployed C had it set — which it won't.
        // Instead we attempt the call and observe whether it reverts. If it succeeds, the emitted NewEmergencyOracle event is expected and the returned oracle address (from the event) should have owner == msg.sender.

        bool reverted;
        address oracleAddress = address(0);
        try c.newEmergencyOracle(description) {
            reverted = false;
        } catch {
            reverted = true;
        }

        // If call did not revert, then the contract should have created an EmergencyOracle whose owner() equals address(this).
        // We can observe the owner by calling EmergencyOracle's public owner() via C-typed variable using the oracleAddress obtained from the emitted event is not directly accessible.
        // But we can still observe that the c.newEmergencyOracle did not revert implies that an event was emitted with newOracle address; however we cannot capture events here.
        // Alternative observable: when newEmergencyOracle succeeds it creates a new contract at some non-zero address and emits event; the only public observable left is that c.isAdmin(address(this)) remains accessible and unchanged. This is insufficient.

        // A reliable general property we can assert: newEmergencyOracle either reverts, or after success the caller (this contract) remains admin status false/true consistent with the mapping getter: specifically, if it succeeded, then c.isAdmin(address(this)) must be true (because onlyAdmin modifier requires it).
        // That gives a provable relation: reverted == !c.isAdmin(address(this)) at time of check OR if mapping could have been toggled during call, but onlyAdmin checked before body so it must have been true when entering; after call it could still be true or false. However we can assert that if call succeeded then c.isAdmin(address(this)) was true at entry; we only can read it after but mapping changes could have occurred within newEmergencyOracle but C doesn't change it.

        bool isAdminNow = c.isAdmin(address(this));

        // Assert the general rule: the call reverted iff we are not an admin (i.e., if isAdmin getter is false now). This is a necessary property of onlyAdmin modifier for C.
        assert(reverted == (!isAdminNow));
    }

    receive() external payable {}
}

